<title>PAKISTAN: PAKISTAN'S HUBCO RISES 1.07 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>PAKISTAN'S HUBCO RISES 1.07 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Hub Power Co Ltd 10-rupee stock rose 0.60 rupee, or 1.07 percent, to 56.50 on Thursday after the company announced a 7,340 million rupee net profit for the year to June, dealers said.</p>
<p>The company, which set up a power house near Karachi, started full 1,292 megawatt power generation in March 1997, dealers at the Karachi Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The scrip rose as it has shown good results and its future prospects are &quot;very good&quot;, dealer Ziana Nowsherwan said.</p>
<p>Some 22 million shares changed hands in early trade.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
